== 2026-10-23
  printed: The term duck curve was coined in 2012 by the California Independent System Operator, and the curve is named for its visual similarity to the outline of a duck. Grid operators hope batteries help the duck keep its neck in check.
  sources line: [Wikipedia, Duck curve](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duck_curve).
  item fact printed as stored: The term duck curve was coined in 2012 by the California Independent System Operator, and the curve is named for its visual similarity to the outline of a duck.
  item second printed as stored: Grid operators hope batteries help the duck keep its neck in check.
  source [fact] Wikipedia, Duck curve raw present; span in the raw file: The curve is named for its visual similarity to the outline of a duck. Used in utility-scale electricity generation, the term was coined in 2012 by the California Independent System Operator.

