== 2026-11-12
  printed: The term horsepower was adopted in the late 18th century by Scottish engineer James Watt to compare the output of steam engines with the power of draft horses. The Citroën 2CV is named for its French fiscal horsepower rating, deux chevaux (2CV).
  sources line: [Wikipedia, Horsepower](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Horsepower).
